      "**A preposition at the end.** In everyday speech, the preposition usually goes at the end: *Who are you waiting for? Where are you from?* *For whom are you waiting?* sounds very formal. When *who* or *what* is the subject, there's no *do*: *Who called?* (see the lesson “Who called you? Subject questions”).",
